{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-446218-r4513923","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Ata Ekuru (Ekuru Sauce)","sourcePageId":446218,"sourceRevision":"4513923","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-19T01:42:11Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Ata%20Ekuru%20(Ekuru%20Sauce)&oldid=4513923","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T12:22:55.272Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Easy recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes using Scotch bonnet chile","Category:Recipes using beef","Category:Recipes using cayenne","Category:Recipes using dehydrated broth","Category:Recipes using fish","Category:Recipes using ground crayfish","Category:Recipes using red bell pepper","Category:Recipes using salt","Category:Recipes with images","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"e87123a8b019d7bb91469f913608f6e943cfb3f5492aa108b2b908293d519ea8","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Sauce recipes\n| Difficulty = 2\n| Image = [[File:Pepper sauce.jpg|300px]]\n}}\n\n{{recipe}}\n\n'''Ata ekuru''' (\"ekuru pepper\"), or '''obe ekuru''' (\"ekuru sauce\"), is a red sauce used to garnish [[Cookbook:Ekuru (White Bean Pudding)|ekuru]]. It is an essential part of ekuru.\n\n== Ingredients ==\n*4 pieces tatase (red [[Cookbook:Bell Pepper|bell peppers]])\n*6 pieces rodo (scotch bonnet [[Cookbook:Chiles|chiles]])\n*10 pieces shombo (fresh [[Cookbook:Cayenne Pepper|cayenne pepper]])\n*1 alubosa ([[Cookbook:Onion|onion]])\n*400 ml [[Cookbook:Palm Oil|palm oil]]\n*[[Cookbook:Bouillon Cube|Seasoning cubes]]\n*Salt\n*Fish (optional)\n*[[Cookbook:Ground Crayfish|Ground crayfish]] (optional)\n*[[Cookbook:Beef|Beef]] (optional)\n*[[Cookbook:Ponmo|Ponmo]] (optional)\n\n== Procedure ==\n#Combine the bell pepper, chiles, and cayenne pepper. Blend to a chunky paste.\n#Heat the palm oil in a [[Cookbook:Frying Pan|pan]]. After about 5 minutes, add the blended pepper mixture to the hot oil. Season with salt and bouillon cubes to taste, and add any of the optional ingredients as desired.\n#Let cook over medium-low heat for about 30–40 minutes, until well-cooked and the oil is floating on top of the sauce.\n#Serve with ekuru.\n\n[[Category:Recipes using beef]]\n[[Category:Recipes using red bell pepper]]\n[[Category:Recipes using Scotch bonnet chile]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cayenne]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ground crayfish]]\n[[Category:Recipes using dehydrated broth]]\n[[Category:Recipes using salt]]\n[[Category:Recipes using fish]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Ata Ekuru (Ekuru Sauce)","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"4 pieces tatase (red bell peppers)","sourceText":"4 pieces tatase (red bell peppers)","amountText":"4 pieces tatase (red bell peppers)","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"6 pieces rodo (scotch bonnet chiles)","sourceText":"6 pieces rodo (scotch bonnet chiles)","amountText":"6 pieces rodo (scotch bonnet chiles)","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"10 pieces shombo (fresh cayenne pepper)","sourceText":"10 pieces shombo (fresh cayenne pepper)","amountText":"